	<key>readme</key>
	<string>t &lt;T-number or words&gt; — find a CXTasks task.

  t 69 / t T69     that task; a prefix like t T11 lists T11, T110…T119
  t &lt;words&gt;        keyword + semantic search (local Ollama nomic-embed-text), fused
  t                what is in motion, most recently touched first

↩ opens the task in CXTasks (cxtasks://task/&lt;id&gt;)
⌘ shows the notes · ⌥ shows tags, repo, tripwire
⇧ or ⌘Y previews the whole task · ⌘L large type · ⌘C copies the T-number

Source: ~/Projects/cxtasks/integrations/alfred — Alfred runs an installed copy,
so re-run install.sh after editing. The semantic lane is optional: without
Ollama the list is built from the number and keyword lanes.</string>
